{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a7f14d4c60fa5d35","name":"Bolotaur","source":{"id":"source:reference-a7f14d4c60fa5d35","title":"Bolotaur","revision":16323,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:42Z","sha256":"720a39771025691e52530f78e59dfe3888c0c15fef0917d1f3d120afe1ebb80f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16323","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Bolotaur&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a7f14d4c60fa5d35","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Bolotaurs are large, long, reptilian creatures native to the forest planet of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"},". A Bolotaur has a long neck ending in an iguanalike face. Beneath the Bolotaur's short snout dangles a brightly colored wattle, used both to attract mates and to scare off competitors. The tail of a Bolotaur is at least as long as the rest of its body, giving it unshakable balance. A Bolotaur moves in a quick, waddling gait, and the claws on its stubby legs dig in and grip the tough bark of the massive trees of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"},", allowing it to climb through the canopies. Bolotaurs range throughout the entire planet, with slight variations in color and in the length of neck and tail.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Bolotaurs are born in clutches of three to five. They have incredibly fast metabolisms, so they must spend most of their day eating. Bolotaurs grow sluggish if they cannot eat every few hours. This fast metabolism greatly reduces their life span, so Bolotaurs live only around twelve years. Although the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wookiees"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wookiees"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Kashyyyk"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kashyyyk","referenceId":"reference:0886d73261c13472"}," occasionally use Bolotaurs, their enemies, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Trandoshans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trandoshans"},", capture Bolotaurs by the thousands and employ them as mounts to hunt down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Wookiees"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Wookiees"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Bolotaur Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +5; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 16, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 11\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 63, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 21\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children"